<title>EGYPT: Egypt mill posts 10-mnth 96/7 profits.</title>
<headline>Egypt mill posts 10-mnth 96/7 profits.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central and West Delta Flour Mills said in an advertisement published on Sunday it had raised net pre-tax profits for the first 10 months of 1996/7 to 60.8 million pounds ($17.9 million) from 37.9 million in the same period of the previous 1995/6 financial year.</p>
<p>The year begins on July 1.</p>
<p>The firm also said it had increased the capacity of six of its mills to a total 2,050 tonnes of wheat a day from 1,500 tonnes per day.</p>
<p>The state privatised about 55 percent of Central and West Delta Mills last year and its shares are among the most popular on the bourse. On Sunday, the stock was trading at about 89.5 pounds.</p>
<p>($1=3.395 Egyptian pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
